### Dhaka Tesla Pool: the story as runnable HTTP calls.
### Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each call.
### Start the API first: `docker compose up -d db` (repo root), then `npm run dev` (apps/api).
### Cookies are remembered between calls, so signing in as someone makes the next calls theirs.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api/v1

### Is everything up?
GET http://localhost:4000/health

### The zones, and what Nusrat's trip will cost before she books (৳100 solo, ৳75 pooled)
GET {{api}}/fares/estimate?pickup=BANANI&dropoff=MOHAKHALI

### 08:41, Banani Road 11. Nusrat signs in...
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nusrat@teslapool.test", "password": "banani0841" }

### ...and books Banani → Mohakhali
# @name nusratBooks
POST {{api}}/rides
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pickupZone": "BANANI", "dropoffZone": "MOHAKHALI", "seats": 1 }

### Her ride, with its timeline
GET {{api}}/rides/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}

### Her active rides
GET {{api}}/rides?scope=active

### Rafiq signs in (his cookie replaces Nusrat's)...
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "rafiq@teslapool.test", "password": "banani0841" }

### ...and tries to look at Nusrat's ride: 404, as if it didn't exist
GET {{api}}/rides/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}

### Back to Nusrat, who cancels (she found a CNG)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nusrat@teslapool.test", "password": "banani0841" }

###
POST {{api}}/rides/{{nusratBooks.response.body.ride.id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Found a CNG instead" }
